<Article
  title="GTA 6 Tree Effigy Locations: Kirk's Search for Tree Effigies"
  h1="GTA 6 Tree Effigies: Where to Find Them (with Screenshots)"
  description="Where to find the tree effigies in Kirk's GTA 6 side quest Search for Tree Effigies, with map and in-game screenshots, how to start it and how to inspect each one."
  published="2026-11-20"
  crumbs={[{ href: "/gta-6/", label: "GTA 6" }]}
  faq={faq}
  sources={[
    { href: "https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/strangers/search-for-tree-effigies", label: "GTABase: Search for Tree Effigies" },
    { href: "https://www.powerpyx.com/?p=372182", label: "PowerPyx: Search for Tree Effigies walkthrough" },
    { href: "https://www.powerpyx.com/?p=372183", label: "PowerPyx: Help Kirk Find Mr. Mangrove" },
  ]}
>
  <p><strong>Search for Tree Effigies</strong> is the second quest for Kirk, the Skunk Ape hunter. He wants photos of 3 carved tree effigies so he can work out where "Mr. Mangrove" is hiding. All three are inside the pink search circle he puts on your map, but they blend into the trees and are easy to walk past. Screenshots below are from our own playthrough.</p>
  <div class="callout"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> fly to <strong>Gullet Marsh</strong> (between Watson Bay and Hamlet), check the pink circle, and look for tall figures built into trees in the mangrove groves. Hold <strong>L2 / LT</strong> to inspect each one. The quest ends when you've inspected all 3.</p></div>

  <h2>How to start it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Finish Kirk's first quest, <strong>Search for the Skunk Ape</strong>.</li>
    <li>Keep playing until Kirk texts you. It can take a while, so do other missions or side activities meanwhile.</li>
    <li>His text adds a large pink search circle over the swamps. You can play it as Jason or Lucia.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tree effigy location: Gullet Marsh, north edge of the circle</h2>
  <p>This was the last one we found, and the hardest to spot. It's at the <strong>north edge of the search circle</strong>, just south of the <strong>Pelican River</strong>, in a patch of dry ground covered by mangrove trees. Open the map once you're close and the effigy marker shows with a distance counter.</p>
  {shots.map((s, i) => (
    <figure style="margin:20px 0">
      <img src={s.src} alt={s.alt} width="1140" height="641" loading={i === 0 ? "eager" : "lazy"} decoding="async" style="border-radius:8px" />
      <figcaption><small>{s.cap}</small></figcaption>
    </figure>
  ))}

  <h2>The other two effigies</h2>
  <p>The other two are also inside the same pink circle, in the open grassland part of the marsh. They're much easier to spot from a distance than the one above. We're adding their exact spots and screenshots next.</p>

  <h2>Tips for finding them</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Use a seaplane.</strong> Fly low over the circle to spot effigies from the air, then land on the marsh water. A <a href="/gta-6/map/">map of Leonida</a> helps you plan the route.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the map often.</strong> The effigy marker only shows up once you're close.</li>
    <li><strong>Look up.</strong> They're as tall as the trees around them, so they're easy to mistake for a trunk.</li>
    <li><strong>No reward money.</strong> It's for 100% completion and Kirk's story. His next quest, Help Kirk Find Mr. Mangrove, is only available as Lucia.</li>
  </ul>
